WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.240
As Halloween 2017 fast approaches, so does
the highly anticipated second season of Stranger

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.380
Things, Matt and Ross Duffer's addictive blend
of Steven Spielberg and Stephen King.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.839
The Netflix thriller became the unexpected
hit of 2016 and propelled its young cast members

00:00:13.839 --> 00:00:17.730
to levels of fame they couldn't have dreamed
of when they answered that first casting call.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.369
But what are the kids of Hawkins, Indiana
like away from the cameras?

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:24.710
This is what the cast of Stranger Things looks
like in real life.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.210
Millie Bobby Brown

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.140
Brown was born in Spain to English parents
and spent her childhood between the UK and

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.140
the US.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.830
Before winning the part of psychokinetic runaway
Eleven, Brown had made a few minor TV appearances,

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.649
though Stranger Things was her first major
gig.

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:42.100
"Is your mom here?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.420
Your dad?"

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:46.820
"Mouthbreather."

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.930
As the breakout star of the show, she quickly
booked a part in Universal's Godzilla sequel,

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:54.110
King of the Monsters, set for release in 2019.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:58.450
While Stranger Things Season 2 details remain
scarce, the first promotional images released

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:02.680
confirm that the Eggo-loving Eleven will no
longer be sporting her laboratory buzz cut,

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.440
instead rocking some very '80s curls.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.440
Finn Wolfhard

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.550
In his role as Mike Wheeler, Finn Wolfhard
took center stage alongside his mysterious

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:14.800
houseguest Eleven, showcasing an impressive
range for such a young actor — impressive

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.580
enough to land him a part in the upcoming
'80s-set adaptation of Stephen King horror

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.980
classic It.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:20.980
"Wow.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.850
She looks…"

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.140
"Pretty… good.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.590
You look pretty good."

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.580
In real life, the curly-haired Canadian is
an indie music aficionado who plays guitar

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.680
and even has his own band.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.390
Gaten Matarazzo

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:40.180
Even though he had stage experience, Gaten
Matarazzo had only a single screen credit

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.820
to his name when he auditioned for the part
of the lovable Dustin Henderson in Stranger

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:44.820
Things.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.820
"Where are you going?

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:46.820
You just said, 'Stick to the plan!'"

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.820
"I am!

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.050
I'm just going to go get some chocolate pudding.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.390
I'm telling you: Lunch lady Phyllis hoards
that s---."

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:55.370
But his lack of screen time wasn't for lack
of trying: The New Jersey-born actor suffers

00:01:55.370 --> 00:02:00.030
from a mild case of cleidocranial dysplasia,
a condition where you're born without a collarbone,

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.950
which affects skull growth and teeth.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.950
Matarazzo used his post-Stranger Things fame
to raise awareness of the condition and received

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.710
countless letters of support after he revealed
that his disability stopped him from getting

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.300
parts for a number of years.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:15.410
But the Duffer Brothers wrote his condition
in, giving his character Dustin the same condition

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:18.770
and even allowing bullies to use it as ammunition
in the show.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.110
Caleb McLaughlin

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.070
Like Matarazzo, Caleb McLaughlin began his
career as an actor on the stage, playing the

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:29.670
young version of Simba in the Broadway production
of The Lion King from 2012 to 2014.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.560
He came into Stranger Things with a couple
of TV credits, like most of his on-screen

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.480
friends, but getting the part of Lucas Sinclair
in Stranger Things was the hardest audition

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.190
process he's been through yet.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:43.590
While his character Lucas is the skeptic of
the group and is initially wary of El, McLaughlin

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.260
revealed that, off-camera, the cast clicked
"like magnets."

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.260
Noah Schnapp

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.960
Schnapp originally auditioned for the role
of Mike Wheeler, but was equally excited to

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.320
learn he'd won the part of Will Byers when
he got a phone call from the Duffer Brothers

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.620
while away at camp.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.569
Schnapp made his film debut in Steven Spielberg's
2015 movie Bridge of Spies — not a bad first

00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:02.660
gig for such a young actor.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:06.370
Schnapp went on to voice Charlie Brown in
The Peanuts Movie before landing the part

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.370
of Will.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.200
Schnapp suspects Will won't quite be himself
in the second season.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.430
The actor told The Hollywood Reporter he thinks
Will is going to "become evil" in Season 2.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:19.000
And seriously, if barfing up slugs during
dinner doesn't make you evil, what does?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.690
Natalia Dyer

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:24.720
Dyer's Stranger Things character Nancy Wheeler
starts out as your typical '80s high school

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.720
girl.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.330
But by the first season's end, she's far from
a teen stereotype, diving head first into

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.830
the Upside Down in search of her missing friend
Barb.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:35.750
She told Cosmopolitan it was "really nice"
to see a character like Nancy, saying, quote,

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:39.980
"She does have that love triangle and boy
drama aspect to her, but she's independent

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:43.620
and strong, and her main focus is about finding
her best friend and solving that mystery at

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.100
any cost."

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.280
Joe Keery

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.020
While Steve Harrington gets under your skin
at the start, his change of heart and obvious

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:54.380
remorse come as unexpected and somewhat refreshing
— and even actor Joe Keery didn't see the

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.420
switcheroo coming.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.230
The cast members were given the scripts episode
by episode, and had little idea about the

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.520
fate of their characters.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.370
Keery was certain he wouldn't be around for
the second season after his questionable behavior

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.320
early in the story, telling Marie Claire he
was sure he'd be "monster food."

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.860
Fortunately, he lived to the end of the season
— and even became something of a cult-favorite

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:15.709
among fans of that other popular show set
in Indiana, Parks and Recreation.

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:17.780
"You guys heard about this fan theory.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:24.840
They think that Steve is actually John Ralphio's
real father."

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.250
Charlie Heaton

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.500
When they're not teaming up with Nancy to
try and rescue Will and Barb from the Upside

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:34.090
Down, Jonathan and Steve compete for her affections
— and in very different ways.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:38.070
While Steve is the confident, popular type,
Jonathan admires Nancy from a distance with

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:41.910
his long-lens camera, earning himself a reputation
as a bit of a creep.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:45.600
Their love triangle looks set to continue
in season two, but even if Jonathan isn't

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.750
quite as prominent this time around, we'll
be seeing a lot more of Heaton regardless.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:54.740
The British actor has been cast as the superhero
Cannonball in Fox's upcoming X-Men spin-off

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:55.990
New Mutants.

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:57.340
Shannon Purser

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.940
Let's finish things off with fan-favorite
Shannon Purser, who looks radically different

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.270
when she's not covered in a thick layer of
pure 1980s.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.120
Barb was a minor character in Stranger Things,
who vanishes pretty early on after being left

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.190
alone outside by Nancy while she hooks up
with Steve... and shows up again at the end

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:16.130
of the season when her body is seen in the
Upside Down, an unfortunate victim of the

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.130
Demogorgon.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:20.900
Despite that, Barb became inexplicably popular
among Stranger Things fans.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.930
The "Justice For Barb" hashtag began trending
on Twitter after her character was killed

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.720
off, and she became one of the most popular
Halloween costumes of 2016.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.321
Purser told the Guardian that some truly dedicated
fans went one step further in their tributes

00:05:29.321 --> 00:05:30.321
to the character, sending her pictures of
Barb's face tattooed on their bodies.

00:05:30.321 --> 00:05:33.130
And while Barb's fate seems pretty much sealed
at the end of season one, some dedicated fans

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.300
still hold out hope that she'll return for
the follow-up.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.600
Hey...stranger things have happened.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.610
Thanks for watching!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.980
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.199
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

